WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.899 --> 00:00:04.890
It was a moment of joy in Abidjan.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:13.719
Supporters of former president Laurent Gbagbo
were watching the ICC decision:

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:18.660
Gbagbo supporters and members of his FPI party
feel as if they've been vindicated.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:25.779
But the old divisions in the country haven't
healed yet:

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:29.462
His acquittal concerns the whole of the Ivory
Coast, because today we must look toward what

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:35.200
is ahead for the country, that's why we're
saying: "Ivory Coast first".

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.540
It was precisely this slogan 'Ivory Coast
first' that contributed to post-electoral

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.750
violence and bloodshed in 2010 and 2011.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:51.320
The Gbagbo camp had alleged that the current
president, Alassane Ouattara, wasn't of Ivorian

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.320
descent.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:57.570
The lawywers representing the current government
at the ICC are skeptical that the decision

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:05.110
to acquit Gbagbo will bring reconciliation
to the Ivory Coast.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.640
3,500 deaths and no one is guilty?

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:15.430
That's going to be unbelievable for the Ivorian
people, and also for the international community.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:20.500
The wife of Laurent Gbagbo, herself pardoned
by President Ouattara, says that the country

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:25.080
needs to forget for its own good.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:30.360
Pardoning isn't a luxury -- pardoning is a
necessity for the Ivory Coast.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.680
Everyone should understand -- whatever their
political party, ethnicity or religion they

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:40.110
need to understand and all the national and
international political players also should

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:45.610
understand this: if this country does not
succeed in pardoning past acts and is not

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:49.560
able to achieve reconciliation, this country
will explode.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.909
This country will disappear.

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:57.450
It is everyone's duty and everyone's responsibility.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:04.190
Speculation have already begun that Laurent
Gbagbo will run in the 2020 presidential election.

